{"availability":"available","full":"hale-lang/hale","name":"hale","description":"A general-purpose, native, memory-safe language for scripts, services, and systems. As a program grows, ownership, concurrency, placement, and effects become things the compiler checks, not conventions.","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":38,"forks":2,"created":"2026-05-15T02:57:23Z","updated":"2026-10-04T21:09:08Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://hale-lang.org","topics":["agents","compiler","concurrency","effect-system","formal-verification","llvm","low-latency","message-passing","model-checking","no-gc","programming-language","static-analysis","systems-programming","wasm"],"demo":"https://hale-lang.org/playground","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T21:35:05.254Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T21:35:05.254Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T21:35:05.254Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:41.270Z","stars":38,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-04T21:35:05.254Z","stars":38,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A locus is a system: made of smaller systems, serving a larger one. It is the unit of Hale's one recursive structural model, and that model holds its shape at every scale: a value, a component, a service, an application, a fleet of running binaries. When a boundary closes, Hale checks the model it can derive and emits evidence that the next scale out composes.","(Precisely: one model, not one syntactic form. A constitution and a fleet plan are not locus declarations — the plan is JSON. What recurs is the account of ownership, flow, closure, and law that each of them is a projection of.)","Most languages stop at the top of the file. Above that line your architecture stops being code and becomes diagrams, deployment YAML, and review comments that no compiler ever reads. Hale keeps going: the same construct describes a value and a deployment, so one checker walks both."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hale-lang/hale/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"662ae27ca0ab84b70cca27b454bc083944dab7ccb1a332d3cd5d87a9c8fdd025","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T22:13:41.382Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T21:36:10.324Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A locus is a system: made of smaller systems, serving a larger one. It is the unit of Hale's one recursive structural model, and that model holds its shape at every scale: a value, a component, a service, an application, a fleet of running binaries. When a boundary closes, Hale checks the model it can derive and emits evidence that the next scale out composes.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hale-lang/hale/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"Architecture is a property of the whole graph: \"billing must never reach research\", \"exactly one thing writes settlements\", and saying that with per-function contracts means scattering them across every position and hoping you got them all.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hale-lang/hale/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"optional","text":"Six forms cover the shapes worth stating. forbid reaches(A, B) for absence, optionally narrowed via { calls } or via { bus }; require subscribes(some G, topic T) for existence; count publishers(topic T) B { publish T; } for a reviewable boundary inventory; and bound llm <= N on paths from G for cost. bound counts a user-declared effect class (effect llm;): the counted…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hale-lang/hale/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"The proven core, all of it self-hosted by the native compiler: the typed topic bus; placement, bindings and NUMA-aware topology with replicas; @form collections; structural interfaces; @ffi C bindings; the fallible(T) error model; effects and budgets; claims, constitutions and fleet composition; the canonical model (hale model, its diff and its verification); record and…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hale-lang/hale/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"662ae27ca0ab84b70cca27b454bc083944dab7ccb1a332d3cd5d87a9c8fdd025","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hale-lang/hale/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T21:36:10.325Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T21:09:08Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hale-lang/hale/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T21:36:10.326Z","hash":"662ae27ca0ab84b70cca27b454bc083944dab7ccb1a332d3cd5d87a9c8fdd025","originalBytes":29852,"storedBytes":29852,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["hale","one","locus","model","every","same","main","what","bus","compiler","nothing","topic","check","each","fleet","get","loci","call","form","pay","there","across","function","language","placement","program","research","run","scale","where","graph","mcp","memory","never","node","out","region","room","they","whole","write","because","build","docs","faster","how","json","only","over","single","system","them","topology","type","which","async","binary","contracts","gameregion","law","lsp","own","pool","publish","rather","reaches","read","runs","service","source","thread","through","typed","agents.md","application","being","bench","billing","bindings","boundary","broadcast","browser","calls","canonical","changes","claims","code","coding","compiled","component","compose","deployment","install","int","ledger","library","license","linux","lock","make","messages","models","msg","name","next","one.","path","per","pinned","plan","programs","reach","release","runtime","shared","slower","string","surface","syscall","under","unix","vec","verification","walks","while","written","about","above","agent","altitude","any","architecture","audit","before","binaries","block","book","carries","chat","checked","checks","closure","collections","compile","contains","count","describe","describes","design","deterministic","diff","dispatch","dna","doc","edito